From a959a32ba083d286a3f21eec93fffb49fb4b58a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:50:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] a11y(ui): label icon-only action buttons in clientes table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Editar and Eliminar buttons in the clientes table contain only an SVG
icon; their accessible name came solely from the `title` attribute, which
screen readers are inconsistent about announcing. VoiceOver + NVDA both
prefer `aria-label` and fall back to inner text — without either, the
button is announced as just "button".

Add `aria-label` that includes the client name so the user knows which
client each button acts on (e.g. "Editar cliente María Pérez"). The
`title` is kept for the visual tooltip.
---
 src/routes/clientes/+page.svelte | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/routes/clientes/+page.svelte b/src/routes/clientes/+page.svelte
index 31bd9da..45e478e 100644
--- a/src/routes/clientes/+page.svelte
+++ b/src/routes/clientes/+page.svelte
@@ -299,6 +299,7 @@
 						<button
 							class="p-2 rounded-lg text-text-secondary hover:text-primary hover:bg-primary/10 transition-colors"
 							title="Editar"
+							aria-label="Editar cliente {c.nombreCompleto}"
 							onclick={() => abrirEditar(c)}
 						>
 							<svg
@@ -319,6 +320,7 @@
 							<button
 								class="p-2 rounded-lg text-text-secondary hover:text-peligro hover:bg-peligro/10 transition-colors"
 								title="Eliminar"
+								aria-label="Eliminar cliente {c.nombreCompleto}"
 								onclick={() => {
 									eliminarId = c.id;
 									eliminarNombre = c.nombreCompleto;
-- 
